WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.336
-Even as
the Russia investigation

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.638
reportedly nears
its first possible indictment

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.706
of a Trump associate,

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.374
the GOP is insisting

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.176
on ramming through
a radical plan

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.711
to repeal Obamacare

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.412
without even waiting
to find out what it does.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.848
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:17.850 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.186 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.555
Of course,
with everything else going on,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.223
Trump has also
been preoccupied lately

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:26.125
with the North Korean
nuclear program.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.993
And since it seems
like threats and sanctions

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.996
have not stopped North Korean
leader Kim Jong-Un so far,

00:00:30.996 --> 00:00:33.232
Trump is trying out
a new tactic -- nicknames.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.901
Over the weekend, he tweeted...

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.740
And then today,
he repeated the nickname,

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.977
not in a tweet,
but in his first speech

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.279
to the United Nations
General Assembly.

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:50.349
-The United States has
great strength and patience,

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:53.852
but if it is forced to defend
itself or its allies,

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:55.855
we will have no choice

00:00:55.855 --> 00:01:00.326
but to totally destroy
North Korea.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:04.397
Rocket Man is on
a suicide mission for himself

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.199
and for his regime.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.002
-Why are you calling him
Rocket Man?

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.838
That's not a diss.
That's a cool nickname.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.639
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:16.876
You're making him sound like
a character from "Top Gun."

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.010
[ As Trump ] Hey.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.780
Hey, Rocket Man,
you're on a suicide mission,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.115
and there's only one way
to settle this --

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.018
on the volleyball court.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:28.021
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.689
[ Normal voice ] So Trump --

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:34.027
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.030
Trump is again threatening
North Korea with military force

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.166
even though that seems to have
failed as a strategy so far.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.333
In fact, as we know,

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:43.669
Trump loves
talking about the military.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.137
He's surrounded himself
with generals,

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:47.139
called for massive increases
in military spending,

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.408
and during a meeting

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.643
with French President
Emmanuel Macron yesterday,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.211
Trump talked
about how much he loved

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:54.347
France's Bastille Day
military parade

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.049
and suggested he might want
to replicate it

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.918
here in the U.S.
on the 4th of July.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.203
Trump talks about the military

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.839
like a kid who just got home
from his first air show.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.640
[ As Trump ] We had a lot
of planes going overhead

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.109
and one of them did a flip

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.410
and another one made a boom,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.579
and then when we landed,
one of the pilots,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.381
he tossed me his sunglasses,
and he said,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.049
"Hey, kid,
I'll see you in the skies."

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.485
And then I said,
"Thanks, Rocket Man."

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.487
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.590
[ Applause ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.660
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
it might be a little foolhardy

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.095
to make plans for next July,

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.730
considering the speed with which
the Russia investigation

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.532
is engulfing
Trump's White House.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.966
Yesterday
was yet another bombshell

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:49.768
about the Russia investigation
being conducted

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:51.737
by special counsel
Robert Mueller,

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.772
suggesting that Mueller
may be close to indicting

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:55.541
one of Trump's
closest associates,

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.177
his former campaign chief,
Paul Manafort.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.311
-Breaking news tonight

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:01.413
on special counsel
Robert Mueller's case

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:02.949
against Paul Manafort.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:06.152
According to<i> The New York Times,</i>
when federal agents executed

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:09.422
a search warrant on Manafort's
Virginia home two months ago,

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.524
which was reported
more recently,

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.760
the special counsel followed up
with a warning.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.630
His prosecutors told Manafort
they planned to indict him.

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.184
-"They even photographed

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.586
the expensive suits
in his closet."

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.620
-That's right.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.656
They photographed
his expensive suits.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.691
Well, Manafort might
like to shop at Armani,

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.126
but where he's headed

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.828
is definitely more
of a men's warehouse.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.229
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.530
[ Applause ]

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.568
Now, the hard-nosed tactics
being used by Mueller

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:58.805
have been described by some
as a shock and awe approach

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.572
with one former
independent counsel saying

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:02.442
Mueller's approach
is intended to scare people

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.610
into telling him the truth.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:11.617
And if there's anyone
who can strike terror

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.118
in the hearts of people
in Washington,

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:14.620
it's Robert Mueller.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.921
Look at him.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.524
He looks like the door-knocker
on a haunted castle.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.827
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:23.762
Another former prosecutor said
the investigation resembled

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:26.365
the way law enforcement has
historically gone after the mob,

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:27.400
telling the<i> Times...</i>

00:04:37.809 --> 00:04:39.511
And that is so unfair.

00:04:39.511 --> 00:04:40.879
How dare anyone call

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:42.915
the Trump administration
organized!

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:43.949
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.318
They're basically --

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:47.353
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:52.624
Come on.
"Organized."

00:04:52.624 --> 00:04:55.694
They're basically running
the government like a Roomba.

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.930
"Yeah, we just go
until we hit a wall

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.465
and then go somewhere else,

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.835
and we suck the whole time."

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.837
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.873
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.176
So, with
the Russia investigation

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:12.511
escalating rapidly,

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.546
how is the president's
legal team responding?

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:16.682
Well, yesterday,
<i> The New York Times</i> reported

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:17.883
that there are
internal divisions

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:19.151
between Trump's lawyers

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:21.553
over how much to cooperate
with the special counsel.

00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:22.955
Trump's lawyer, Ty Cobb,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.324
has accused the White House
counsel Don McGahn,

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.760
together known as
"Franklin and 'Stache,"

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.862
of withholding
sensitive information

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.497
from the rest of the team.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.232
According to the<i> Times,</i>
Cobb said of McGahn...

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.671
The craziest part, though,
is how<i> The New York Times</i>

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.272
found out about Cobb's comments.

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:41.740
It wasn't from an interview
or an anonymous source.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.775
Instead...

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.552
The Trump administration
is worried about leaks,

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.254
and yet, it keeps hiring people

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:58.691
who are the physical
manifestation of leaks.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.692
When they talk,
it should just be the sound

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:03.095
of air escaping a balloon.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:05.131
[ Air hissing,
balloon screeching ]

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:12.338
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:14.339
[ Applause ]

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:17.176
Now, obviously,
we don't know yet

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.543
where the Russia investigation
will lead,

00:06:18.543 --> 00:06:19.679
but one thing's for sure.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.414
It will continue
to infuriate Trump,

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:24.183
who remains obsessed
with both the 2016 election

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.219
and, in particular,
Hillary Clinton,

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.686
so much so that he retweeted

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:29.622
a video from a fan account
over the weekend

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.056
that made it look like
he hit Hillary

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:32.925
in the back with a golf ball.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.193
Hey man,
I don't know if you noticed,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.595
but you're the one
under FBI investigation

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.096
with approval ratings
in the low 30s.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:40.199
If you're gonna post memes
of yourself golfing,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.101
at least make them
more accurate.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.840
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.876
[ Applause ]

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:55.814
And, yet...

00:06:55.814 --> 00:06:57.516
he was so happy to swallow --

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:58.985
he's so happy to eat
a golf ball.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.352
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:01.654
And yet,
even with these scandals

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.689
swirling around a historically
unpopular president,

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:04.824
Trump's party is still trying

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.892
to push through
his domestic agenda,

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:10.596
specifically his promise
to repeal and replace Obamacare.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.698
The GOP is like your friend

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:15.201
who knows only one song
on the guitar

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:17.403
and he's drunk
and no one wants to hear it,

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.738
but he's tuning it up again.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.907
Republicans are pushing a new
bill that is in many ways

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:23.208
even more radical
than previous bills.

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:24.243
The new bill...

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.092
Although last week,

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.927
when Trump first heard about
the new GOP health care bill

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:43.295
being advanced in the Senate,

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:45.565
he talked about it
in vague terms and made clear

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.099
he had no idea what it was.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:50.102
-We'll be discussing probably
a little bit of health care,

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.972
because I know some
information's come to light.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:55.407
-"Some information's come
to light."

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:57.075
Every time Trump talks
about health care,

00:07:57.075 --> 00:08:00.446
he sounds like a teaser trailer
for a soap opera.

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.582
Next week
on an all new "Trumpcare"...

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:06.118
-We had to go
with the health care first,

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.320
and we're doing well.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.555
I think we're gonna have
some great surprises.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.891 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:14.460
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.763
-What kind of surprises?

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.899
This latest attempt to ram
through a health care bill

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:22.301
that would literally take money
away from vulnerable people

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.603
without letting people know
what it would do

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:26.405
is why Democrats need
to be extremely careful

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.908
before making any deals
with Trump and the GOP.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:30.576
Trump has apparently
commented recently

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:31.944
that it's much easier
to get along

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:34.646
with Democratic leaders
Chuck Schumer and Nancy Pelosi

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:37.315
than with GOP leaders
Paul Ryan and Mitch McConnell.

00:08:37.315 --> 00:08:39.385
According to Politico,
Trump has dismissed Ryan as...

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:50.529
Oh, I wish I could see Trump
trying to make small talk

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:51.831
with Mitch McConnell.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:55.100
[ As Trump ]
Do you have a gold apartment?

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.937
[ As McConnell ]
I do not, Mr. President.

00:08:57.937 --> 00:08:59.572
[ As Trump ] Oh.

00:08:59.572 --> 00:09:01.607
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.545
Why does your face
look like that?

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:08.414
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:09.682
[ Normal voice ]
Meanwhile, after a meeting

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:11.517
between Trump and Schumer,
his fellow New Yorker,

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:12.785
a congressman who was present

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:14.620
said Trump and Schumer
got along so well...

00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:19.491
...and Schumer was caught
on a hot mic on the Senate floor

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:22.428
gushing about how much
Trump likes the Democrats

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:24.096
and him, in particular,
even telling a colleague

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:26.799
that his new partnership
with Trump would go smoothly.

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:47.419
-No!
It won't work out!

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:50.156
He'll only be your ally as long
as you're useful to him.

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.957
Haven't you seen how he treats
his friends?

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:54.293
First, you'll stand behind him
at a press conference,

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:56.228
and the next thing you know,
you're eating nachos

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:59.164
and yelling at people
at baseball games.

00:09:59.164 --> 00:10:02.167
It's a precipitous ball.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:05.304
Remember, this is still
the same Donald Trump

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:07.106
who ran a cruel,
bigoted campaign,

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:08.507
who called Mexicans rapists,

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:10.008
bragged about committing
sexual assault,

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:11.176
and fired the FBI director

00:10:11.176 --> 00:10:12.778
for investigating
his administration.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.180
In fact, just last week

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.814
after an attack
on the London Underground,

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:17.516
before any details were known,

00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:20.286
Trump doubled down on his call
for a Muslim travel ban.

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:21.320
-Trump tweeting...

00:10:30.495 --> 00:10:31.764
-And then there was this.

00:10:40.605 --> 00:10:43.208
-"Must be proactive and nasty"?

00:10:43.208 --> 00:10:46.612
That's not a terrorism strategy.
That's a Prince "B" side.

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:47.946
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.946 --> 00:10:49.314
You know what,
can we actually hear

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:51.217
a little "Proactive and Nasty"?

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:56.255
-♪ I'm not gonna wait
for that ass to come to me ♪

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.989
♪ Unh ♪

00:10:57.989 --> 00:10:59.224
♪ Yeah ♪

00:10:59.224 --> 00:11:03.095
♪ I'm about to get
proactive and nasty ♪

00:11:03.095 --> 00:11:04.263
-That's it.

00:11:04.263 --> 00:11:06.265
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:08.768
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:11.303
So, one of Trump's
closest associates

00:11:11.303 --> 00:11:12.672
is on the verge
of being indicted,

00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:14.373
and the GOP is trying
to ram through

00:11:14.373 --> 00:11:16.008
a massively unpopular bill

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:17.676
that could strip health care
away from millions.

00:11:17.676 --> 00:11:18.877
I'll say it again.

00:11:18.877 --> 00:11:20.813
Donald Trump is really hitting
a hole in one.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.384
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.384 --> 00:11:28.821
Right into his own mouth.
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:30.622 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:30.622 --> 00:11:32.425 line:0%
♪♪

